DESCRIPTION >
    - `repositoryStarSnapshots` contains aggregate-only star count snapshots for repositories.
    - Replicated from Postgres - one row per repository per snapshot run, no per-user stargazer identity.
    - `id` is the primary key identifier for the snapshot record.
    - `repositoryId` links to the repository this snapshot belongs to.
    - `starCount` is the aggregate star count captured at `capturedAt`.
    - `capturedAt` is when the snapshot was taken.
    - `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are standard timestamp fields for record lifecycle tracking.

SCHEMA >
    `id` String `json:$.record.id`,
    `repositoryId` String `json:$.record.repositoryId`,
    `starCount` Int32 `json:$.record.starCount`,
    `capturedAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.capturedAt`,
    `createdAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.createdAt`,
    `updatedAt` DateTime64(3) `json:$.record.updatedAt`

ENGINE ReplacingMergeTree
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY toYear(createdAt)
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY repositoryId, capturedAt
ENGINE_VER updatedAt
